<!--
  HexCursor bootstrap UI Context. Registered via <AddUserInterfaces
  context="InGame"> in CivViAccessMod.modinfo. Civ VI's engine InGame.lua
  iterates Modding.GetUserInterfaces("InGame") and calls LoadNewContext on
  each — that loads this XML and (by convention) the same-named
  HexCursorAddin.lua alongside it, giving us our own ContextPtr that
  receives keyboard input.

  Cannot shadow InGame.lua directly ("MODs / Expansions cannot use partial
  replacement as this context is directly added to the UI Control Tree via
  engine"). Cannot use PlotToolTip's context for input — it's mouse-only.
  AddUserInterfaces is the engine-blessed extension point.

  No UI controls defined here on purpose — HexCursor is an invisible
  cursor + input handler. The Context exists solely to host the Lua side.
-->
<Context>
</Context>
